# Only what the image's build reads goes to Docker, as for the API
# (backend/.dockerignore): not node_modules (the image installs the packages
# itself; those from Windows would not work in Linux), not dist (it builds the
# page itself), and no file kept on this computer only, such as .env.local or
# a test report. tsc -b checks e2e and the config files too (tsconfig.node.json).
*
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!.npmrc
!index.html
!src
!public
!e2e
!nginx.conf
!vite.config.ts
!eslint.config.js
!playwright.config.ts
!tsconfig*.json
